 acquisition — open file A, open file B, ",[36,1551,1552],{"class":194},"`defer b.Close()`",[36,1554,58],{"class":50},[36,1556,1557],{"class":194},"`defer a.Close()`",[36,1559,1560],{"class":50},". LIFO ensures B (opened last) is closed first, matching resource lifetimes.\n",[36,1562,1563,1565,1567,1570,1572,1575,1577,1580,1582,1585,1588,1591,1594,1597,1599,1602,1605],{"class":38,"line":249},[36,1564,260],{"class":42},[36,1566,1362],{"class":42},[36,1568,1569],{"class":50},"Debug",[36,1571,1368],{"class":42},[36,1573,1574],{"class":50},": ",[36,1576,1027],{"class":194},[36,1578,1579],{"class":50}," arguments are evaluated at ",[36,1581,321],{"class":42},[36,1583,1584],{"class":50}," time, not at execution time — ",[36,1586,1587],{"class":194},"`defer fmt.Println(i)`",[36,1589,1590],{"class":50}," prints the value of ",[36,1592,1593],{"class":194},"`i`",[36,1595,1596],{"class":50}," when ",[36,1598,1027],{"class":194},[36,1600,1601],{"class":50}," was called, not when it runs. To capture the later value, use a closure: ",[36,1603,1604],{"class":194},"`defer func() { fmt.Println(i) }()`",[36,1606,1414],{"class":50},[36,1608,1609],{"class":38,"line":254},[36,1610,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1612,1613,1616,1618],{"class":38,"line":274},[36,1614,1615],{"class":50},"## ⚠️ Edge Cases ",[36,1617,1348],{"class":42},[36,1619,1620],{"class":50}," Gotchas\n",[36,1622,1623],{"class":38,"line":280},[36,1624,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1626,1627,1629,1631,1633,1636,1638,1640,1643],{"class":38,"line":286},[36,1628,260],{"class":42},[36,1630,1362],{"class":42},[36,1632,1027],{"class":194},[36,1634,1635],{"class":50}," in a loop",[36,1637,1368],{"class":42},[36,1639,1574],{"class":50},[36,1641,1642],{"class":194},"`for ... { defer f.Close() }`",[36,1644,1645],{"class":50}," accumulates deferred calls until the function returns — resources pile up. Close inside the loop, or refactor the loop body into a function.\n",[36,1647,1648,1650,1652,1654,1657,1659,1662,1665,1668,1670,1673,1675,1677,1679,1682,1685,1687,1690,1692,1695,1697,1699,1702,1704,1706,1709,1711],{"class":38,"line":292},[36,1649,260],{"class":42},[36,1651,1362],{"class":42},[36,1653,1027],{"class":194},[36,1655,1656],{"class":50}," and loops ",[36,1658,85],{"class":42},[36,1660,1661],{"class":50}," closures (",[36,1663,1664],{"class":175},"1.22",[36,1666,1667],{"class":50}," fix)",[36,1669,1368],{"class":42},[36,1671,1672],{"class":50},": pre",[36,1674,260],{"class":42},[36,1676,1664],{"class":175},[36,1678,58],{"class":50},[36,1680,1681],{"class":194},"`for i := 0; ... { defer func() { fmt.Println(i) }() }`",[36,1683,1684],{"class":50}," printed the ",[36,1686,678],{"class":42},[36,1688,1689],{"class":50},"final",[36,1691,678],{"class":42},[36,1693,1694],{"class":50}," value of ",[36,1696,1593],{"class":194},[36,1698,1030],{"class":42},[36,1700,1701],{"class":50}," all iterations (loop variable captured by reference). Go ",[36,1703,1664],{"class":175},[36,1705,85],{"class":42},[36,1707,1708],{"class":50}," makes each iteration",[36,1710,1489],{"class":194},[36,1712,1713],{"class":1492},"s loop variable distinct, fixing this. On older Go, pass `i` as an argument: `defer func(i int) { ... }(i)`.\n",[36,1715,1716],{"class":38,"line":301},[36,1717,1718],{"class":1492},"- **Naked returns in long functions**: `return` (no values) in a 100-line function with named returns is opaque — readers must scan for where the named returns were set. Use naked returns only in short functions.\n",[36,1720,1721],{"class":38,"line":307},[36,1722,1723],{"class":1492},"- **`defer` has a small overhead**: each `defer` has a tiny cost (function call + stack bookkeeping). In hot paths (millions of iterations), it can matter — Go 1.14+ optimized the common case (open-coded defer) to near-zero, but `defer` in a loop still adds up.\n",[36,1725,1726,1729,1731,1734,1737,1739,1742,1745,1747,1750,1753],{"class":38,"line":1097},[36,1727,1728],{"class":1492},"- **Multiple returns must be fully received or discarded**: `f, err := os.Open(...)` — you must use both (or `_`). You can",[36,1730,1489],{"class":194},[36,1732,1733],{"class":50},"t receive only one of a multi",[36,1735,1736],{"class":42},"-return",[36,1738,1574],{"class":50},[36,1740,1741],{"class":194},"`f := os.Open(...)`",[36,1743,1744],{"class":50}," is an ",[36,1746,891],{"class":42},[36,1748,1749],{"class":50},". Use ",[36,1751,1752],{"class":194},"`f, _ := ...`",[36,1754,1755],{"class":50}," to discard explicitly.\n",[36,1757,1759,1761,1763,1766,1769,1771,1773,1776,1779,1782,1785,1788,1791,1794,1797,1799],{"class":38,"line":1758},25,[36,1760,260],{"class":42},[36,1762,1362],{"class":42},[36,1764,1765],{"class":194},"`...`",[36,1767,1768],{"class":50}," spread requires a slice, not a single value",[36,1770,1368],{"class":42},[36,1772,1574],{"class":50},[36,1774,1775],{"class":194},"`sum(nums...)`",[36,1777,1778],{"class":50}," where ",[36,1780,1781],{"class":194},"`nums`",[36,1783,1784],{"class":50}," is ",[36,1786,1787],{"class":194},"`[]int`",[36,1789,1790],{"class":50}," works; ",[36,1792,1793],{"class":194},"`sum(5...)`",[36,1795,1796],{"class":50}," doesn",[36,1798,1489],{"class":194},[36,1800,1801],{"class":1492},"t. The `...` is the spread operator for variadic calls.\n",[36,1803,1805,1808,1810,1813,1815],{"class":38,"line":1804},26,[36,1806,1807],{"class":1492},"- **Function types are distinct**: `func(int) int` and `func(int64) int` are different types — you can",[36,1809,1489],{"class":194},[36,1811,1812],{"class":50},"t assign one to the other. This matches Go",[36,1814,1489],{"class":194},[36,1816,1817],{"class":1492},"s no-implicit-conversion rule.\n",[36,1819,1821],{"class":38,"line":1820},27,[36,1822,1823],{"class":1492},"- **Closures capture by reference**: `for i := 0; i \u003C 3; i++ { go func() { fmt.Println(i) }() }` (pre-1.22) prints \"3 3 3\" — all goroutines see the final `i`. Pass `i` as an argument: `go func(i int) { ... }(i)`.\n",[36,1825,1827,1830,1832,1835,1838,1840,1842,1845,1848,1850],{"class":38,"line":1826},28,[36,1828,1829],{"class":1492},"- **`defer` doesn",[36,1831,1489],{"class":194},[36,1833,1834],{"class":50},"t run on ",[36,1836,1837],{"class":194},"`os.Exit`",[36,1839,1368],{"class":42},[36,1841,1574],{"class":50},[36,1843,1844],{"class":194},"`os.Exit(n)`",[36,1846,1847],{"class":50}," terminates immediately without running deferred functions. Don",[36,1849,1489],{"class":194},[36,1851,1852],{"class":1492},"t call `os.Exit` inside a function with cleanup `defer`s — return an error and let `main` exit.\n",[36,1854,1856],{"class":38,"line":1855},29,[36,1857,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1859,1861],{"class":38,"line":1860},30,[36,1862,1863],{"class":1492},"## 🧠 Spot the Bug\n",[36,1865,1867],{"class":38,"line":1866},31,[36,1868,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1870,1872],{"class":38,"line":1871},32,[36,1873,1874],{"class":1492},"A developer opens files in a loop to process them, but runs out of file descriptors:\n",[36,1876,1878],{"class":38,"line":1877},33,[36,1879,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1881,1883],{"class":38,"line":1882},34,[36,1884,1885],{"class":1492},"::code-wrapper{language=\"go\"}\n",[36,1887,1889],{"class":38,"line":1888},35,[36,1890,277],{"class":1492},[36,1892,1894],{"class":38,"line":1893},36,[36,1895,1896],{"class":1492},"func processFiles(paths []string) error {\n",[36,1898,1900],{"class":38,"line":1899},37,[36,1901,1902],{"class":1492},"    for _, p := range paths {\n",[36,1904,1906],{"class":38,"line":1905},38,[36,1907,1908],{"class":1492},"        f, err := os.Open(p)\n",[36,1910,1912],{"class":38,"line":1911},39,[36,1913,1914],{"class":1492},"        if err != nil {\n",[36,1916,1918],{"class":38,"line":1917},40,[36,1919,1920],{"class":1492},"            return err\n",[36,1922,1924],{"class":38,"line":1923},41,[36,1925,1926],{"class":1492},"        }\n",[36,1928,1930],{"class":38,"line":1929},42,[36,1931,1932],{"class":1492},"        defer f.Close()   \u002F\u002F ❌ deferred until processFiles returns\n",[36,1934,1936],{"class":38,"line":1935},43,[36,1937,1938],{"class":1492},"        \u002F\u002F process f...\n",[36,1940,1942],{"class":38,"line":1941},44,[36,1943,396],{"class":1492},[36,1945,1947],{"class":38,"line":1946},45,[36,1948,1949],{"class":1492},"    return nil\n",[36,1951,1953],{"class":38,"line":1952},46,[36,1954,94],{"class":1492},[14,1956,312],{},[14,1958,1959],{},"What's wrong?",[1961,1962,1963,1967,1981,1990,1996,2169,2179],"details",{},[1964,1965,1966],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1968,1969,1972,1973,1976,1977,1980],{},[33,1970,1971],{},"defer f.Close()"," doesn't run until ",[33,1974,1975],{},"processFiles"," returns — so all files stay open for the duration of the loop. With many files, you exhaust file descriptors (",[33,1978,1979],{},"EMFILE: too many open files",").",[14,1982,1983,1985,1986,1989],{},[33,1984,321],{}," is function-scoped, not block-scoped. In a loop, deferred calls accumulate; they only run when the enclosing ",[1107,1987,1988],{},"function"," returns, not at the end of each iteration.",[14,1991,1992,1993,1995],{},"The fix — extract the loop body into a function so each ",[33,1994,321],{}," runs per iteration:",[27,1997,1999],{"className":29,"code":1998,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"func processFiles(paths []string) error {\n    for _, p := range paths {\n        if err := processFile(p); err != nil {\n            return err\n        }\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc processFile(path string) error {\n    f, err := os.Open(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    defer f.Close()   \u002F\u002F runs when processFile returns — per file\n    \u002F\u002F process f...\n    return nil\n}\n",[33,2000,2001,2024,2038,2059,2066,2070,2074,2081,2085,2089,2107,2119,2131,2137,2141,2154,2159,2165],{"__ignoreMap":31},[36,2002,2003,2005,2008,2010,2013,2015,2018,2020,2022],{"class":38,"line":39},[36,2004,43],{"class":42},[36,2006,2007],{"class":46}," processFiles",[36,2009,51],{"class":50},[3